          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "page-template"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Page Template\n\nA page is a graph of pieces. Each piece is a node of a role class (masthead, route, section) and the page is **the pieces in graph order**.\n\nThe Method *Assemble the page* stacks the pieces into one document and writes it into the Declaration's exposed views. One Handler per role and one for the graph structure keep that view current, so adding, removing, reordering or editing a piece redraws the page with no extra wiring.\n\nStart by editing the example pieces. The page you are building is the Detail view."
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
